  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Oral health is one of the major problems in Bhutan, but many health workers at PHCs and district level are not aware of the common oral health disorders. To increase early detection of oral health problems we must build the capacity of health professionals. Describe 2 resource-smart approaches to build the capacity of health professionals. (1.5x2 marks)', '(1) Integrate oral health into existing training: add a short module on common oral diseases (dental caries, gum disease, oral cancer and precancerous lesions, oral infections) into existing in-service training, CMEs and refresher courses for health assistants and nurses, and use online/ virtual sessions and simple pictorial screening guides and checklists, so no separate costly training is needed. (2) Training of trainers and mentoring: dental surgeons and dental hygienists at regional and district hospitals train a few focal persons, who then train staff at PHCs (cascade training); this is supported by supportive supervision visits, on-the-job mentoring and tele-dentistry (sending photos for advice), which builds skills and early referral at low cost.', null, '[{"point": "Approach 1 (e.g. integrate oral health into existing in-service training/ CME and use online or virtual training and the national e-learning platform, with simple screening checklists and pictorial guides)", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Approach 2 (e.g. training of trainers/ cascade training by dental surgeons and dental hygienists at district level, supportive supervision, mentoring and tele-dentistry consultation)", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
