  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Name two occupational health diseases commonly seen in Bhutan. Name the most appropriate diagnostic test for diagnosis of respiratory diseases. (1+2 marks)', 'Occupational diseases seen in Bhutan include dust-related lung diseases such as silicosis/ pneumoconiosis among workers in mines, quarries, stone-crushing units and construction, and noise-induced hearing loss in industrial workers; others are musculoskeletal disorders (back pain), pesticide poisoning in farmers and needle-stick infections among health workers. The most appropriate diagnostic test for respiratory diseases is spirometry (pulmonary function test), which measures FEV1 and FVC to show obstructive or restrictive lung disease; a chest X-ray (and sputum examination for infection) supports the diagnosis.', null, '[{"point": "Two occupational diseases, e.g. pneumoconiosis/ silicosis (mining, quarrying, stone crushing), occupational asthma/ dust-related lung disease, noise-induced hearing loss, musculoskeletal disorders/ back pain, pesticide poisoning, needle-stick infections in health workers", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Diagnostic test: spirometry (lung function test) for respiratory diseases, with chest X-ray (and sputum tests) as supporting tests", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
