  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Draw and label an animal cell. List a function each of 2 organelles. (2+1 marks)', 'Diagram (described): a rounded cell bounded by a thin plasma membrane, with cytoplasm containing a large central nucleus (with nuclear membrane, nucleolus and chromatin), rod-shaped mitochondria with folded inner membranes (cristae), rough endoplasmic reticulum studded with ribosomes, smooth endoplasmic reticulum, free ribosomes, a stack of Golgi apparatus, small lysosomes, a centrosome with two centrioles near the nucleus and small vacuoles; there is no cell wall, chloroplast or large central vacuole. Functions: the nucleus contains DNA and controls all the activities of the cell; mitochondria are the ''powerhouses'' that release energy as ATP by aerobic respiration (others: ribosomes make proteins, Golgi apparatus packages and secretes proteins, lysosomes digest waste and worn-out parts).', null, '[{"point": "Labelled diagram: cell (plasma) membrane, cytoplasm, nucleus with nucleolus and nuclear membrane, mitochondria, rough and smooth endoplasmic reticulum, ribosomes, Golgi apparatus, lysosomes, centrosome/ centrioles, vacuole (small)", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Functions of any 2, e.g. nucleus controls the cell and holds DNA; mitochondria make ATP (aerobic respiration); ribosomes make proteins; Golgi packages proteins; lysosomes digest waste", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
