  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'The ultrasound scan is a commonly used diagnostic test in modern medical practice. What is the principle of ultrasound scan? (3 marks)', 'An ultrasound scan uses very high-frequency sound waves (usually 2-18 MHz, far above the human hearing limit of 20 kHz). A probe (transducer) containing piezoelectric crystals converts electrical energy into sound pulses and sends them into the body; gel is used so there is no air between the probe and skin. When the sound waves meet boundaries between tissues of different density (acoustic impedance), part of the wave is reflected back as an echo - this is the pulse-echo principle. The same crystals receive the echoes and convert them into electrical signals; the time taken for an echo to return shows the depth of the structure and its strength shows the brightness, so a computer builds a real-time picture. It uses no ionising radiation, so it is safe in pregnancy, and the Doppler effect is used to measure blood flow.', null, '[{"point": "Ultrasound: high-frequency sound waves (about 2-18 MHz, above 20 kHz) produced by a piezoelectric transducer (probe) that both sends and receives", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Pulse-echo principle: waves pass into the body and are reflected (echoes) at boundaries between tissues of different acoustic impedance; gel removes air", "marks": 1}, {"point": "The time taken for echoes to return gives depth and their strength gives brightness; a computer forms a real-time image; no ionising radiation, safe in pregnancy; Doppler measures blood flow", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
